[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186159374 :answer-field/choices 17592186159376] [:db/retract 17592186159374 :answer-field/choices 17592186159375] {:db/id 17592186162362 :question/problem "![](images/93/931f7cc1fe4cc6a45c1f586bb017bb3eda8f7745aa3973c13f08aa8521c39400.png)\n\nA $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere $\\{x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ The corresponding ellipse and its principal axes are depicted in the diagram above. Given that ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A,$ what are the nonzero singular values of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix. Let \n\n$$\n\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\,…,{v}_{n}\\}\n$$\n\nbe an *orthonormal* basis of ${R}^{n}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A$ with corresponding eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}\\ge {\\lambda }_{2}\\ge …\\ge {\\lambda }_{n}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{1},$\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nIn our example, we see that\n\n- $||A{v}_{1}||=4={\\sigma }_{1},$ and\n\n- $||A{v}_{2}||=2={\\sigma }_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the nonzero singular values of $A$ are ${\\sigma }_{1}=4$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159374 :answer-field/correct 17592186159379 :answer-field/choices ["answer-38f9c426-dab0-57b7-aa76-6f687589b344" "answer-585850a0-2e98-5454-a5ce-c2c74b29b565"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38f9c426-dab0-57b7-aa76-6f687589b344" :answer/id #uuid "38f9c426-dab0-57b7-aa76-6f687589b344" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4{v}_{1}$ and $2{v}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-585850a0-2e98-5454-a5ce-c2c74b29b565" :answer/id #uuid "585850a0-2e98-5454-a5ce-c2c74b29b565" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{1}$" :db/ensure