n that ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A,$ what are the nonzero singular values of $A?$"] [17592186162362 :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix. Let \n\n$$\n\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\,…,{v}_{n}\\}\n$$\n\nbe an *orthonormal* basis of ${R}^{n}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A$ with corresponding eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}\\ge {\\lambda }_{2}\\ge …\\ge {\\lambda }_{n}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{1},$\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nIn our example, we see that\n\n- $||A{v}_{1}||=4={\\sigma }_{1},$ and\n\n- $||A{v}_{2}||=2={\\sigma }_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the nonzero singular values of $A$ are ${\\sigma }_{1}=4$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=2.$"] [17592186162362 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-38f9c426-dab0-57b7-aa76-6f687589b344" :answer/id #uuid "38f9c426-dab0-57b7-aa76-6f687589b344"] ["answer-38f9c426-dab0-57b7-aa76-6f687589b344" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-38f9c426-dab0-57b7-aa76-6f687589b344" :answer/value "$4{v}_{1}$ and $2{v}_{1}$"] ["answer-585850a0-2e98-5454-a5ce-c2c74b29b565" :answer/id #uuid "585850a0-2e98-5454-a5ce-c2c74b29b565"] ["answer-585850a0-2e98-5454-a5ce-c2c74b29b565" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-585850a0-2e98-5454-a5ce-c2c74b29b565" :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{1}$"] [17592186159374 :answer-field/correct 17592186159379] [17592186159374 :answer-field/choices "answer-38f9c426-dab0-57b7-aa76-6f687589b344"] [17592186159374 :answer-field/choices "answer-585850a0-2e98-5454-a5ce-c2c74b29b565"] ["activity-8c4631f5-ce38-50ca-8db4-4b2dd080d0df" :activity/id #uuid "8c4631f5-ce38-50ca-8db4-4b2dd080d0df"] ["step-ec8da15c-64b8-543b-87b6-4d2e08009505" :step/id #uuid "ec8da15c-64b8-543b-87b6-4d2e08009505"] ["step-7935da3a-469b-5bce-9e33-166b16dfa9be" :step/id #uuid "7935da3a-469b-5bce-9e33-166b16dfa9be"] ["step-45611da9-d3af-5cc7-b007-af7ba19a6423